# Rosetta native corpus exclusions: files in native.index that one port does not run.
#
#   <port>[:<runner>]  <file>  <reason>
#
# port:   c python swift rust go zig java kotlin csharp csharp-bid
# runner: core wrapper net11 (net11: the csharp / csharp-bid Decimal128.Net11.Rosetta
#         program). Without a runner, the file is excluded from every runner of
#         that port.
# reason: required, the rest of the line. Remove the line when the reason no
#         longer holds.
#
# Example:
#   csharp:net11  transcsweep.txt  runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48
#
# Checked by rosetta/check_native.py (run by CI).

# The D48 files (D48SwiftWorkOrder.md D-6, Phase 4, Phase 6): the transcendental
# sweeps, the corrected compound/rootn vectors and the pown/rootn oracle vectors.
# Every port runs them since its D48 switch (D-7). Only the net11 runners exclude
# them: they drive .NET 11's own Decimal128, not the port's D48.
csharp:net11     transcsweep.txt  runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpWorkOrder.md CS-18)
csharp:net11     transcstress.txt runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpWorkOrder.md CS-18)
csharp:net11     transcfix.txt    runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpWorkOrder.md CS-18)
csharp:net11     transcoracle.txt runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpWorkOrder.md CS-18)
csharp-bid:net11 transcsweep.txt  runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpBidWorkOrder.md CB-7)
csharp-bid:net11 transcstress.txt runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpBidWorkOrder.md CB-7)
csharp-bid:net11 transcfix.txt    runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpBidWorkOrder.md CB-7)
csharp-bid:net11 transcoracle.txt runs .NET 11's own Decimal128, not this port's D48 (D48CsharpBidWorkOrder.md CB-7)

# transccompound.txt (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md CX-6): compound lines a port
# that rounds 1 + x to 34 digits before the power gets wrong. Remove a port's line
# in that port's compound commit; the net11 runners then keep a `:net11` line.
rust             transccompound.txt compound still rounds 1 + x to 34 digits (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)
go               transccompound.txt compound still rounds 1 + x to 34 digits (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)
zig              transccompound.txt compound still rounds 1 + x to 34 digits (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)
java             transccompound.txt compound still rounds 1 + x to 34 digits (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)
kotlin           transccompound.txt compound still rounds 1 + x to 34 digits (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)
csharp           transccompound.txt compound still rounds 1 + x to 34 digits (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)
csharp-bid       transccompound.txt compound still rounds 1 + x to 34 digits (CompoundD48OnePlusXWorkOrder.md)
